Transitive components
---------------------

The transitive closure of the components above (Netty, Guava, Protocol Buffers, gRPC,
Apache Hadoop and Parquet client libraries pulled in by Tika and Flink, Jetty, PDFBox, and
others) is also bundled. Their license texts and notices are carried inside the jar under
META-INF/ (META-INF/LICENSE*, META-INF/NOTICE*, META-INF/licenses/ and
META-INF/license/) because the shade plugin keeps those resources. Run
`unzip -l target/agentic-flink-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT-uber.jar | grep META-INF/maven/` for the
complete list of bundled Maven coordinates in a given build.

The other modules of the reactor (ports/jagentic-core, agentic-pekko, pyflink/java,
tool-services-packs) build thin jars and bundle no third-party code. The Quarkus modules
(tool-services/tool-services-app, and a2a-gateway behind the a2a-gateway profile) build a
target/quarkus-app/ directory whose lib/ folder holds the dependency jars unchanged, each
with its own license files.

The Python distributions (pyagentic, agentic-flink, agentic-pyflink, agentic-pipeline)
bundle no third-party code except that the agentic-flink wheel carries the uber jar
described above as package data (python/setup.py).
